WEBVTT

00:05:58.184 --> 00:06:00.383
In poor communities,
in communities of color,

00:06:00.407 --> 00:06:01.726
there is this despair,

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:03.593
there is this hopelessness

00:06:03.617 --> 00:06:05.725
that is being shaped by these outcomes.

00:06:06.123 --> 00:06:09.255
One out of three Black men
between the ages of 18 and 30

00:06:09.279 --> 00:06:12.726
is in jail, in prison,
on probation or parole.

00:06:13.454 --> 00:06:15.469
In urban communities
across this country --

00:06:15.493 --> 00:06:17.947
Los Angeles, Philadelphia,
Baltimore, Washington --

00:06:17.971 --> 00:06:20.821
50 to 60 percent of all young men of color

00:06:20.845 --> 00:06:22.155
are in jail or prison

00:06:22.179 --> 00:06:23.971
or on probation or parole.

00:06:23.995 --> 00:06:26.321
Our system isn't just
being shaped in these ways

00:06:26.345 --> 00:06:28.385
that seem to be distorting around race,

00:06:28.409 --> 00:06:30.051
they're also distorted by poverty.